---
// THE CHAPTER BREAK — the page's single structural pivot. Everything above it
// is her own work; everything below it is the index. It carries the OPEN
// rhythm step twice over — once as margin, once as padding — which is why it
// stays the largest gap on the page by roughly 2x and why nothing else on the
// page competes with it.
//
// ENTRANCE — the pivot is its own entrance, and it is the second of the two
// SANCTIONED EXCEPTIONS to the three-edge staircase. One element, one edge.
//
// FULL INTERRUPTION (E.8, step 12). It used to sit at .col-body — the exact
// measure of the paragraphs above and below it — so it read as one more block
// in the column rather than as a break in it. It now takes .col-break, a
// column earlier and two later, sharing neither edge with anything it
// interrupts.
//
// HANGING PUNCTUATION. The opening quotation mark hangs LEFT of the text
// edge, so the E of "Every" is what measures flush and what the eye reads as
// the block's left edge. A quote mark sitting inside the measure makes the
// whole block look indented. text-indent, not hanging-punctuation: the
// property is Safari-only and would double-apply there on top of this.
//
// Obsidian ground. Gold on Obsidian is 5.8:1; gold on Porcelain is 2.4:1 and
// on Cashmere 1.9:1, both of which fail even the 3:1 large-text floor, so the
// dark ground is what lets this stay the page's loudest gold moment.
//
// NO HAND-SET grid-column ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE.
---

<section class="pullquote" id="sec-quote">
  <div class="spread">
    <h2 class="col-break">&ldquo;Every decision is viewed through a larger lens: <em>Legacy</em>.&rdquo;</h2>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Full viewport width by nature — a top-level section, never inside .spread.
     The OPEN step sits both outside and inside it. */
  .pullquote{
    margin: var(--vr-open) 0;
    padding: var(--vr-open) 0;
    background-color: var(--obsidian);
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(88% 72% at 78% 10%, rgba(175,140,92,0.13) 0%, rgba(175,140,92,0) 60%),
      radial-gradient(70% 60% at 6% 94%,  rgba(71,68,64,0.58) 0%, rgba(71,68,64,0) 62%);
  }

  /* GOLD 3 of 3 — the page's largest accent. Quote tier: opsz 96, SOFT 40,
     WONK 1. WONK 1 in italic swaps in the flagged ball terminals on b, d, h,
     k, l, v and w. That flourish is the whole reason this tier exists. Axes
     unchanged by this pass. */
  .pullquote h2{
    /* Narrow inside a wide column: the void to its right is what makes the
       block read as hung rather than centred, and .col-break gives it more
       void than .col-body did. */
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    /* Hanging punctuation. -0.42em is the measured advance of U+201C in
       Fraunces italic at this tier, so the line starts a quote-width left and
       the first letter lands exactly on the text edge. */
    text-indent: -0.42em;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variation-settings: var(--fx-quote);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 340;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 112px);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-align: left;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* The closing word carries the section; Porcelain against the gold gives
     the line an internal contrast step without introducing a sixth colour. */
  .pullquote em{
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--porcelain);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px){
    .pullquote h2{ max-width: none; }
  }
</style>
